    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5262" root="جدل" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَجْدَلُ</span></b> ; fem. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَدْلَآءُ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَجْدُولٌ</span>, in three
places ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also, [accord. to most of the grammarians <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَجْدَلٌ</span>, but accord. to some <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَجْدَلُ</span>,] The
<i>hawk;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَقْرٌ</span>; (S, K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَجْدَلِىٌّ</span></b> :
(K:) or an epithet applied to the hawk [and
therefore without tenween]: (TA:) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَجَادِلُ</span>.
(K.)

